.Dd December 25, 2024
.Dt CTFDIFF 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ctfdiff
.Nd compare the SUNW_ctf section of two ELF files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f-ignore-const
.Ar file1
.Ar file2
.Nm
.Cm abi-check
.Fl -base Ar base
.Fl -new Ar new
.Fl -type Ar type
.Op Fl -type Ar type
.Op Fl -types-file Ar path
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -max-reasons Ar n
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility compare the contents of the CTF (Compact C Type Format) data section
(SUNW_ctf) present in two ELF binary files.
This section was previously created with
.Xr ctfconvert 1
or
.Xr ctfmerge 1 .
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl f-ignore-const
Ignore
.Dv const
qualifiers when comparing types.
.El
.Pp
The
.Cm abi-check
subcommand compares ABI slot compatibility in a directional manner from
BASE to NEW for the requested types.
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -base Ar base
Base ELF file to compare against.
.It Fl -new Ar new
New ELF file to check for compatibility.
.It Fl -type Ar type
Type name to check (repeatable).
For example,
.Qq struct bio .
.It Fl -types-file Ar path
Read type names from a file, one per line.
.It Fl -json
Emit machine-readable JSON output.
.It Fl -max-reasons Ar n
Limit the number of breaking reasons reported per type (default 20).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It 0
All requested types are compatible.
.It 1
At least one type is incompatible.
.It 2
Usage or tool error (missing files, CTF parse failure, etc.).
.It 3
At least one type is unknown due to missing or insufficient info.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ctfconvert 1 ,
.Xr ctfmerge 1 ,
.Xr ctfdump 1 ,
.Xr ctf 5
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Fx 15.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
ShengYi Hung <aokblast@FreeBSD.org>
The CTF utilities came from OpenSolaris.
